PentaX modifications, 2026-10-17:
  Ported these portions to safe Rust, replacing unchecked spans and process
  aborts with owned immutable input, typed errors and checked fallible limits.
  Added private instruction records with owner-bound views, bounded allocation
  capacities and work accounting, and original synthetic regression tests.
  Retained source opcode IDs, operand/constant and literal word rules, export
  flags and interpolation operands. Preserved caller-supplied stage metadata.
  Exposed linear-span decoding instead of the original program/termination
  walker. Branch target metadata uses signed arithmetic without wraparound.
  Deferred other families explicitly, without guessing their lengths or
  translating instructions, resources, descriptor bindings or shaders.

PentaX modifications, 2026-10-18:
  Ported the remaining observed families (VOP1/VOP2/VOPC/VOP3/VOP3P, SMEM,
  MUBUF, MTBUF, FLAT, DS and MIMG) with their source opcode maps, aliases,
  SDWA/DPP/DPP8 and VOP3/VOP3P modifier rules, memory/image fields, NSA and
  BVH address counts. Replaced source aborts and SetUnsupported results with
  typed errors in the source's check order, proved every modifier, body, NSA
  and literal word present before reading it, and added compact fixed-size
  operand, memory and image metadata plus original synthetic tests. Opcode
  tables were transcribed into Rust match tables; no C++ is included.

